    "profile_text": {
        "body": "AeroVironment Inc is a publicly traded company, listed under the ticker AVAV, headquartered in Arlington, Virginia. Its own site describes it as a leading manufacturer of Unmanned Aircraft Systems, Unmanned Aerial Vehicles, Loitering Munition Systems, and Unmanned Ground Vehicles used for surveillance and reconnaissance by the United States Military, U.S. allies, and commercial industries. The company also states that it manufactures High-Altitude Pseudo-Satellites.\n\nThe site names MacCready Works as AeroVironment's advanced development group, which it says turns concepts into mission-ready autonomous systems. The group is described as inspired by Dr. Paul B. MacCready, Jr., and staffed by engineers, roboticists, and AI researchers designing next-generation robotic systems across air, land, and sea. The company describes a MacCready Method of building fast, testing relentlessly, and deploying advantage, with small multidisciplinary teams moving ideas into operational capability in months.\n\nThe company's litigation exposure is recorded in Virginia, with a count of 129 cases. No product entries or MCP servers are recorded for it.",
